          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K$ be a smooth oriented embedded circle in the oriented standard three-sphere, let $F$ be a connected compact smooth oriented embedded surface with boundary $K$, and let $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ be any ordered integral basis of $H_1(F;\\mathbb Z)$ with Seifert matrix $V_{ij}=\\operatorname{lk}(a_i^+,a_j)$. Let $J_F$ be the matrix of the algebraic intersection form on $F$, with a transverse intersection of oriented curves $u,v$ counted positively exactly when their ordered tangent vectors form a positive basis of $TF$. Then $V-V^T=J_F$. The matrix $J_F$ is skew-symmetric and unimodular; when $a_1,\\ldots,a_{2g}$ is a standard handle basis, it is a direct sum of blocks $\\begin{psmallmatrix}0&1\\\\-1&0\\end{psmallmatrix}$.",
